Meta.documentation:Number
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:An exact, arbitrary-precision rational number.
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:Numbers are value resources backed by arbitrary-precision rationals — 0.1 +
Meta.documentation:0.2 is exactly 0.3. Literals support decimal (Number:42), fractions
Meta.documentation:(Number:1.5), scientific notation (Number:1.5e2), other bases with #base
Meta.documentation:(Number:FF#16, Number:101#2, bases 2–16), and _ as a thousands separator
Meta.documentation:(Number:1_000_000).
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:Blob interface — in_octetstream_$all parses bytes as a num/den
Meta.documentation:fraction (exact); out_octetstream offers the value in that form. Used by
Meta.documentation:http:, file: and Dawn.cast when loading content.
Meta.documentation:@port in_octetstream_$all — bytes parsed as a num/den fraction
Meta.documentation:@port out_octetstream — the value as a num/den fraction in bytes
Meta.documentation:@example
Meta.documentation:[Number:0.1 Number:0.2]>>Number.add:>>Console:
Meta.documentation:---
Meta.documentation:0.3
